From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 11:53:57 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/vkms: test the stereo modes listed from an EDID

Build a device from the default configuration with vkms_output_init(),
its HDMI-A connector reading an EDID that declares 3D in its HDMI
Vendor-Specific Data Block, and check that:

- the connector lists the stereo modes the EDID declares and no other
  (an EDID with frame packing, top and bottom and side by side (half),
  and one that declares every structure of HDMI 1.4a, Table H-2: line
  alternative, L + depth, L + depth + graphics + graphics-depth and side
  by side (full) too), the expected formats being those edid-decode reads
  from the EDID;
- the writeback connector accepts a buffer of the frame that holds both
  eyes and refuses other sizes, for each layout and for a 2D mode;
- a connector with no EDID lists no stereo mode.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/vkms/tests/Makefile           |   3 +-
 drivers/gpu/drm/vkms/tests/vkms_stereo_test.c | 655 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 657 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 drivers/gpu/drm/vkms/tests/vkms_stereo_test.c

